 transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-72\" transform=\"translate(0 0.90625)\"></use></g></g><g id=\"text_7\"><g transform=\"translate(156.846818 16.011562) scale(0.13 -0.13)\"><defs><path id=\"STIXGeneral-Italic-73\" d=\"M 2342 2829 \nL 2214 1933 \nL 2112 1933 \nQ 2022 2675 1542 2675 \nQ 1370 2675 1267 2579 \nQ 1165 2483 1165 2310 \nQ 1165 2067 1510 1658 \nQ 1946 1152 1946 787 \nQ 1946 397 1686 163 \nQ 1427 -70 1024 -70 \nQ 838 -70 672 -6 \nQ 538 51 390 51 \nQ 262 51 205 -83 \nL 102 -83 \nL 230 934 \nL 333 934 \nQ 461 64 973 64 \nQ 1203 64 1331 192 \nQ 1459 320 1459 557 \nQ 1459 845 1101 1293 \nQ 698 1798 698 2131 \nQ 698 2451 909 2636 \nQ 1120 2822 1472 2822 \nQ 1600 2822 1830 2758 \nQ 1971 2714 2061 2714 \nQ 2189 2714 2253 2829 \nL 2342 2829 \nz\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-73\" transform=\"translate(0 0.796875)\"></use></g></g><g id=\"text_8\"><g transform=\"translate(7.2 23.34995) scale(0.13 -0.13)\"><defs><path id=\"STIXGeneral-Italic-6b\" d=\"M 2950 2739 \nL 2950 2637 \nQ 2720 2624 2464 2448 \nQ 2208 2272 1510 1651 \nL 1747 1088 \nQ 2099 262 2266 262 \nQ 2400 262 2554 531 \nQ 2586 582 2650 698 \nL 2746 627 \nQ 2522 224 2374 77 \nQ 2227 -70 2035 -70 \nQ 1894 -70 1782 42 \nQ 1670 154 1517 454 \nQ 1325 826 1133 1357 \nL 877 1152 \nL 570 0 \nL 90 0 \nL 992 3379 \nQ 1082 3699 1107 3942 \nQ 1088 4096 781 4096 \nL 666 4096 \nL 666 4198 \nQ 1146 4256 1670 4371 \nL 1709 4333 \nL 941 1414 \nL 1216 1626 \nQ 2131 2330 2131 2522 \nQ 2131 2637 1894 2637 \nL 1805 2637 \nL 1805 2739 \nL 2950 2739 \nz\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-6b\" transform=\"translate(0 0.703125)\"></use></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pe4939fe293\"><rect x=\"16.711364\" y=\"20.772678\" width=\"209.25\" height=\"207.9\"></rect></clipPath></defs></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 3 lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled k, r, and s.</li><li>Line k intersects both line r and line s.</li><li>At the intersection of line k and line r, 2 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br><ul><li>Top right: w°</li><li>Bottom right: x°</li></ul></li><li>At the intersection of line k and line s, 2 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br><ul><li>Top right: y°</li><li>Bottom right: z°</li></ul></li><li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p><p>In the figure shown, line $k$ intersects lines $r$ and $s$. If $w=147$, which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that lines $r$ and $s$ are parallel?</p>","choices":[{"label":"A","text":"$x=33$"},{"label":"B","text":"$y=147$"},{"label":"C","text":"$w+y=180$"},{"label":"D","text":"$y+z=180$"}],"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Choice B is correct. The figure shows transversal $k$ intersecting lines $r$ and $s$, where the angles labeled $w^\\circ$ and $y^\\circ$ are two corresponding angles and the angles labeled $x^\\circ$ and $z^\\circ$ are two corresponding angles. When a transversal intersects two lines, the lines are parallel if and only if two corresponding angles are congruent. It’s given that $w=147$. If $y=147$, then the two corresponding angles labeled $w^\\circ$ and $y^\\circ$ are congruent, which is sufficient to prove that lines $r$ and $s$ are parallel.\nChoice A is incorrect. The angle labeled $x^\\circ$ forms a linear pair with the angle labeled $w^\\circ$, so $x=180-147$, or $x=33$, regardless of whether lines $r$ and $s$ are parallel.\nChoice C is incorrect. Substituting $147$ for $w$ in this equation yields $147+y=180$, or $y=33$. Since the angle labeled $w^\\circ$ and the angle labeled $y^\\circ$ are corresponding angles, if $w$ and $y$ aren’t equal, then lines $r$ and $s$ can’t be parallel.\nChoice D is incorrect. The relationship $y+z=180$ describes a linear pair at line $s$, which is true regardless of whether lines $r$ and $s$ are parallel.","is_grid_in":false},{"source_id":"d12bca0a","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Circles","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"A circle in the x y plane with the origin labeled O.\nThe circle shown has its center at $(0,0)$. What is the value of $k$?","question_text_html":"<p><figure><svg id=\"uuid-551f143b-2682-4d52-889b-c07ee2a4104e\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"225.612\" height=\"230.195\" viewBox=\"0 0 225.612 230.195\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A circle in the x y plane with the origin labeled O.\"><path d=\"m0,226.595v-.63h.195c.23,0,.437-.025.623-.075.185-.05.332-.152.442-.308.11-.155.165-.387.165-.697v-7.35c0-.3-.058-.522-.173-.667-.115-.145-.265-.24-.45-.285-.185-.045-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h2.745l5.37,8.295v-6.645c0-.3-.058-.522-.172-.667-.115-.145-.265-.24-.45-.285-.185-.045-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h3.765v.63h-.195c-.22,0-.425.025-.615.075s-.34.15-.45.3c-.11.15-.165.385-.165.705v9h-1.065l-5.625-8.64v6.93c0,.31.055.542.165.697.11.155.26.258.45.308.19.05.395.075.615.075h.195v.63H0Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><path d=\"m15.18,226.745c-1.08,0-1.93-.345-2.55-1.035-.62-.69-.93-1.74-.93-3.15,0-1.4.297-2.442.892-3.127.595-.685,1.473-1.027,2.633-1.027,1.08,0,1.93.343,2.55,1.027.62.685.93,1.728.93,3.127,0,1.41-.298,2.46-.893,3.15-.595.69-1.473,1.035-2.632,1.035Zm.03-.78c.5,0,.9-.127,1.2-.383.3-.255.515-.637.645-1.147.13-.51.195-1.135.195-1.875,0-1.12-.155-1.959-.465-2.52-.31-.56-.84-.84-1.59-.84s-1.277.28-1.583.84c-.305.561-.458,1.4-.458,2.52s.155,1.968.465,2.542c.31.575.84.863,1.59.863Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><path d=\"m23.13,226.745c-.76,0-1.312-.172-1.658-.518s-.518-.947-.518-1.807v-5.01h-1.14v-.6c.18,0,.38-.037.6-.112.22-.075.41-.197.57-.368.17-.18.31-.4.42-.66.11-.26.2-.58.27-.96h.69v1.845h1.965v.855h-1.965v5.055c0,.51.105.885.315,1.125.21.24.485.36.825.36.18,0,.345-.01.495-.03.15-.02.305-.045.465-.075v.66c-.13.0