$ABCD$?</p>","choices":[{"label":"A","text":"$5$"},{"label":"B","text":"$9$"},{"label":"C","text":"$14$"},{"label":"D","text":"$28$"}],"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Choice C is correct. The area, $A$, of a rectangle is given by the formula $A=lw$, where $l$ is the length and $w$ is the width of the rectangle. It's given that rectangle $ABCD$ shown has a length of $7$ units and a width of $2$ units. Substituting $7$ for $l$ and $2$ for $w$ in the formula $A=lw$ yields $A=(7)(2)$, or $A=14$. Therefore, the area, in square units, of rectangle $ABCD$ is $14$.\nChoice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.\nChoice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.\nChoice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.","is_grid_in":false},{"source_id":"30aa51b7","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Area and volume","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"Graph of 4 points in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 8 to 8. The y axis ranges from negative 8 to 8. Refer to long description.\nA rectangle is formed by the four points shown. What is the area, in square units, of the rectangle?","question_text_html":"<p><figure><svg version=\"1.0.0\" width=\"370px\" height=\"336.328125px\" viewBox=\"0 0 370 336.328125\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Graph of 4 points in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 8 to 8. The y axis ranges from negative 8 to 8. Refer to long description.\"><defs><marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 -3 10 6\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"10px\" markerHeight=\"6px\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,-3 L10,0 L0,3\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></marker></defs><g transform=\"translate(25, 25)\"><g><g><line x1=\"156.1640625\" y1=\"311.328125\" x2=\"156.1640625\" y2=\"0\" st