-46\"></path></defs><g transform=\"translate(47.12625 190.368)scale(0.12 -0.12)\"><use xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-78\"></use><use x=\"70.410156\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-111\"></use><use x=\"120.214844\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-116\"></use><use x=\"150.878906\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-101\"></use><use x=\"192.871094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-58\"></use><use x=\"215.917969\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use><use x=\"238.28125\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-70\"></use><use x=\"292.089844\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-105\"></use><use x=\"318.359375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-103\"></use><use x=\"364.648438\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-117\"></use><use x=\"415.136719\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-114\"></use><use x=\"452.246094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-101\"></use><use x=\"494.238281\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use><use x=\"516.601562\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-110\"></use><use x=\"569.628906\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-111\"></use><use x=\"619.433594\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-116\"></use><use x=\"650.097656\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use><use x=\"672.460938\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-100\"></use><use x=\"720.996094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-114\"></use><use x=\"758.105469\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-97\"></use><use x=\"799.414062\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-119\"></use><use x=\"871.09375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-110\"></use><use x=\"924.121094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use><use x=\"946.484375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-116\"></use><use x=\"977.148438\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-111\"></use><use x=\"1026.953125\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use><use x=\"1049.316406\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-115\"></use><use x=\"1084.375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-99\"></use><use x=\"1123.925781\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-97\"></use><use x=\"1165.234375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-108\"></use><use x=\"1189.746094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-101\"></use><use x=\"1231.738281\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-46\"></use></g></g></g></g></g><g transform=\"translate(23, 18) scale(1 1) \"><polygon points=\"192.491 0.945 192.491 146.149 0.945 146.149 192.491 0.945\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><rect x=\"181.151\" y=\"134.809\" width=\"11.34\" height=\"11.34\" stroke-width=\"0.945\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"></rect></g></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for right triangle\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>One angle is a right angle.</li><li>The lengths of the sides adjacent to the right angle are as follows:<ul><li>4</li><li>9</li></ul></li><li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p><p>The figure shows the lengths, in units, of two sides of a triangle. What is the area, in square units, of the triangle?</p>","choices":[{"label":"A","text":"$18$"},{"label":"B","text":"$13$"},{"label":"C","text":"$9$"},{"label":"D","text":"$4$"}],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Choice A is correct. The area, $A$, of a triangle is given by the formula $A=\\frac{1}{2}bh$, where $b$ is the length of the base of the triangle and $h$ is the height of the triangle. In the right triangle shown, the length of the base of the triangle is $9$ units, and its height is $4$ units. Substituting $9$ for $b$ and $4$ for $h$ in the formula $A=\\frac{1}{2}bh$ yields $A=\\frac{1}{2}(9)(4)$, or $A=18$. Therefore, the area of the triangle, in square units, is $18$.\nChoice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.\nChoice C is incorrect. This is the length of the base of the triangle, in units, not the area of the triangle, in square units.\nChoice D is incorrect. This is the height of the triangle, in units, not the area of the triangle, in square units.","is_grid_in":false},{"source_id":"9fdc4eaa","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Area and volume","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"A right square pyramid has a total surface area of $70,560$ square inches, and the combined surface area of the four lateral faces of this pyramid is $38,160$ square inches. What is the height, in inches, of this pyramid?","question_text_html":null,"choices":[{"label":"A","text":"$56$"},{"label":"B","text":"$90$"},{"label":"C","text":"$106$"},{"label":"D","text":"$180$"}],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Choice A is correct. The total surface area of a right square pyramid is the sum of the combined surface area of its four lateral faces and the area of its square base. It’s given that the right square pyramid has a total surface area of $70,560$ square inches, and the combined surface area of the four lateral faces of this pyramid is $38,160$ square inches. It follows that the area of the square base is the difference between the total surface area and the combined surface area of the four lateral faces, or $(70,560-38,160)$ square inches, which is equal to $32,400$ square inches. The area, $B$, of the base of a square pyramid is given by the equation $B=s^2$, where $s$ is the side length of the base. Substituting $32,400$ for $B$ in this equation yields $32,400=s^2$. Taking the positive square root of both sides of this equation yields $180=s$. The four lateral faces of a square pyramid are congruent triangles. It follows that the area of each lateral face is $\\frac{38,160}{4}$ , or $9,540$, square inches. The area, $A$, of each lateral face of a square pyramid is given by the equation $A=\\frac{1}{2}sl$, where $s$ is the side length of the pyramid’s base and $l$ is the pyramid’s slant height. Substituting $9,540$ for $A$ and $180$ for $s$ in this equation yields $9,540=\\frac{1}{2}(180)l$, or $9,540=90l$. Dividing both sides of this equation by $90$ yields $106=l$. In the right square pyramid, a right triangle can be drawn, where the lengths of the legs correspond to the pyramid's height, $h$, and half the side length of its base, $\\frac{1}{2}s$, and the length of the hypotenuse corresponds to the pyramid's slant height, $l$. It follows that the relationship between $h$, $s$, and $l$ is given by the equation $h^2+(\\frac{1}{2}s)^2=l^2$. Substituting $180$ for $s$ and $106$ for $l$ in this equation yields $h^2+((\\frac{1}{2})(180))^2=(106)^2$, or $h^2+8,100=11,236$. Subtracting $8,100$ from both sides of this equation yields $h^2=3,136$. Taking the positive square root of both sides of the equation yields $h=56$. Therefore, the height, in inches, of this pyramid is $56$.\nChoice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.\nChoice C is incorrect. This is the pyramid's slant height, not its height, in inches.\nChoice D is incorrect. This is the side length of the pyramid's base, not its height, in inches.","is_grid_in":false},{"source_id":"f6ca90cc","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Area and volume","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"A right prism has a square base with side lengths of $10$ inches. The height of the prism is $58$ inches. What is the volume, in cubic inches, of the prism?","question_text_html":null,"choices":[],"correct_answer":"5800","explanation":"The correct answer is $5,800$. The volume, $V$, of a right prism with a square base is given by the formula $V=s^2h$, where $s$ is the side length of the square base and $h$ is the height of the prism. It’s given that a right prism has a square base with side lengths of $10$ inches. It's also given that the height of the prism is $58$ inches. Substituting $10$ for $s$ and $58$ for $h$ in the formula $V=s^2h$ yields $V=(10)^2(58)$, or $V=5,800$. Therefore, the volume, in cubic inches, of the prism is $5,800$.","is_grid_in":true},{"source_id":"7a11ceea","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"A diagram of 2 lines and 2 line segments. Refer to long description.\nIn the figure, segment $AD$ and segment $BE$ intersect at point $C$. Segment $AD$ is perpendicular to line $l$ at point $A$. Which of the following additional pieces of information is(are) sufficient to determine that triangle $ABC$ is congruent to triangle $DEC$?\nSegment $AD$ is perpendicular to line $m$ at point $D$.\n$AC=13$ and $DC=13$","question_text_html":"<p><figure><svg id=\"uuid-afc45d29-3c34-41c4-965e-55269b6af215\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"225.612\" height=\"253.808\" viewBox=\"0 0 225.612 253.808\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A diagram of 2 lines and 2 line segments. Refer to long description.\"><path d=\"M0,250.208v-.63h.195c.23,0,.437-.025.623-.075.185-.05.332-.152.442-.308.11-.155.165-.387.165-.697v-7.35c0-.3-.058-.522-.173-.667-.115-.145-.265-.24-.45-.285-.185-.045-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h2.745l5.37,8.295v-6.645c0-.3-.058-.522-.172-.667-.115-.145-.265-.24-.45-.285-.185-.045-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h3.765v.63h-.195c-.22,0-.425.025-.615.075s-.34.15-.45.3c-.11.15-.165.385-.165.705v9h-1.065l-5.625-8.64v6.93c0,.31.055.542.165.697.11.155.26.258.45.308.19.05.395.075.615.075h.195v.63H0Z\"></path><path d=\"M15.18,250.358c-1.08,0-1.93-.345-2.55-1.035-.62-.69-.93-1.74-.93-3.15,0-1.4.297-2.442.892-3.127.595-.685,1.473-1.027,2.633-1.027,1.08,0,1.93.343,2.55,1.027.62.685.93,1.728.93,3.127,0,1.41-.298,2.46-.893,3.15-.595.69-1.473,1.035-2.632,1.035ZM15.21,249.578c.5,0,.9-.127,1.2-.383.3-.255.515-.637.645-1.147.13-.51.195-1.135.195-1.875,0-1.12-.155-1.959-.465-2.52-.31-.56-.84-.84-1.59-.84s-1.277.28-1.583.84c-.305.561-.458,1.4-.458,2.52s.155,1.968.465,2.542c.31.575.84.863,1.59.863Z\"></path><path d=\"M23.13,250.358c-.76,0-1.312-.172-1.658-.518s-.518-.947-.518-1.807v-5.01h-1