605-.585,2.535-.585.89,0,1.575.152,2.055.458.48.305.72.708.72,1.208,0,.36-.135.645-.404.855-.271.21-.625.315-1.065.315,0-.21-.018-.433-.053-.667s-.104-.458-.21-.667c-.104-.21-.254-.38-.449-.51-.195-.13-.458-.195-.788-.195-.55,0-1.053.133-1.508.397-.455.265-.86.62-1.215,1.065-.355.445-.652.948-.893,1.507-.24.561-.422,1.138-.547,1.733-.125.595-.188,1.172-.188,1.732,0,.59.1,1.095.3,1.515.2.42.498.74.893.96.395.22.887.33,1.478.33.71,0,1.288-.142,1.732-.427s.792-.598,1.042-.938c.06.04.107.105.142.195.035.09.053.19.053.3,0,.26-.107.535-.322.825s-.553.533-1.012.728c-.46.195-1.06.292-1.8.292Z\"></path><path d=\"M153.04,144.75l.12-.63h.195c.229,0,.442-.025.638-.075.194-.05.367-.152.517-.308.15-.155.256-.387.315-.697l1.56-7.35c.021-.07.035-.143.046-.217.01-.075.015-.143.015-.203,0-.27-.112-.438-.338-.502-.225-.065-.473-.098-.742-.098h-.195l.136-.63h4.199c1.351,0,2.397.348,3.143,1.042.745.695,1.118,1.708,1.118,3.038,0,.89-.131,1.735-.391,2.535-.26.8-.645,1.508-1.154,2.123-.511.615-1.138,1.098-1.883,1.448s-1.603.525-2.572.525h-4.726ZM157.436,143.984c.739,0,1.399-.147,1.979-.442s1.072-.71,1.478-1.245c.405-.535.713-1.172.923-1.913.21-.74.314-1.55.314-2.43,0-1.1-.257-1.902-.772-2.408-.515-.505-1.207-.757-2.077-.757h-1.185l-1.966,9.195h1.306Z\"></path><path d=\"M121.841,205.933l.12-.63h.194c.22,0,.428-.022.623-.067.194-.045.367-.138.518-.278.149-.14.255-.36.314-.66l1.561-7.365c.02-.07.032-.135.037-.195s.008-.115.008-.165c0-.32-.103-.52-.308-.6s-.453-.12-.743-.12h-.194l.135-.63h7.56l-.479,2.625h-.78c.01-.05.021-.14.03-.27s.02-.257.03-.382c.01-.125.015-.198.015-.218,0-.28-.08-.518-.24-.712s-.435-.292-.825-.292h-2.52l-.855,3.99h3.615l-.149.735h-3.615l-.96,4.485h2.895c.32,0,.59-.058.811-.172.22-.115.402-.265.547-.45.146-.185.258-.387.338-.607l.24-.645h.779l-.659,2.625h-8.04Z\"></path></svg><div role=\"region\" class=\"sr-only\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 2 lines and 2 line segments\"><ul><li>Clockwise from top left, the 2 lines are line script l and line m. </li><li>From bottom to top, point upper A and point upper B are on line script l. </li><li>From bottom to top, point upper E and point upper D are on line m. </li><li>The following line segments are drawn between line script l and line m:<br><ul><li>Segment upper B upper E</li><li>Segment upper A upper D</li></ul></li><li>Segment upper A upper D intersects segment upper B upper E at point upper C.</li><li>The intersections of the lines and line segments form triangle upper A upper B upper C and triangle upper D upper E upper C. <br><ul><li>Triangle upper A upper B upper C has a common vertex with triangle upper D upper E upper C. </li><li>The common vertex is upper C. </li></ul></li><li>Note: Figure not drawn to scale. </li></ul></div></figure></p><p>In the figure, segment $AD$ and segment $BE$ intersect at point $C$. Segment $AD$ is perpendicular to line $l$ at point $A$. Which of the following additional pieces of information is(are) sufficient to determine that triangle $ABC$ is congruent to triangle $DEC$?</p><ol><li>Segment $AD$ is perpendicular to line $m$ at point $D$.</li><li>$AC=13$ and $DC=13$</li></ol>","choices":[{"label":"A","text":"I is sufficient by itself, but II is not."},{"label":"B","text":"II is sufficient by itself, but I is not."},{"label":"C","text":"I is sufficient by itself, and II is sufficient by itself."},{"label":"D","text":"Neither I nor II is sufficient by itself."}],"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Choice D is correct. In the figure, it’s given that segment $AD$ is perpendicular to line $l$ at point $A$. Statement I is that segment $AD$ is perpendicular to line $m$ at point $D$. It follows that angles $BAC$ and $EDC$ are right angles. Therefore, triangles $ABC$ and $DEC$ are right triangles. At least one pair of congruent corresponding sides is needed to determine triangle congruence by the side-angle-side (SAS) condition or the angle-side-angle (ASA) condition, so statement I is not sufficient to determine that triangle $ABC$ is congruent to triangle $DEC$. Statement II is that $AC=13$ and $DC=13$. It follows that triangles $ABC$ and $DEC$ share one pair of congruent corresponding sides. Two additional pairs of congruent corresponding parts are needed to determine triangle congruence by SAS condition, ASA condition, or side-side-side (SSS) condition, so statement II is not sufficient to determine that triangle $ABC$ is congruent to triangle $DEC$. Therefore, neither I nor II is sufficient by itself to determine that triangle $ABC$ is congruent to triangle $DEC$.\nChoice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.\nChoice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.\nChoice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.","is_grid_in":false},{"source_id":"25cc5327","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Area and volume","difficulty":"medium","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"The base of a right rectangular pyramid has a length of $27$ centimeters and a width of $2$ centimeters. The height of this pyramid is $7$ centimeters. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of this pyramid?","question_text_html":null,"choices":[],"correct_answer":"126","explanation":"The correct answer is $126$. It’s given that the base of the right rectangular pyramid has a length of $27$ centimeters and a width of $2$ centimeters and that the height of the pyramid is $7$ centimeters. The volume, $V$, of a right rectangular pyramid is given by the formula $V=\\frac{1}{3}lwh$, where $l$ and $w$ are the length and width, respectively, of the pyramid’s base and $h$ is the height of the pyramid. Substituting $27$ for $l$, $2$ for $w$, and $7$ for $h$ in this formula yields $V=\\frac{1}{3}(27)(2)(7)$, or $V=126$. Therefore, the volume, in cubic centimeters, of the pyramid is $126$.","is_grid_in":true},{"source_id":"858809e7","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"A diagram of 2 lines and 4 line segments. Refer to long description.\nIn the figure, $\\overline{EG}$ and $\\overline{AD}$ intersect at point $F$, and line $l$ is parallel to line $j$. If $EF=0.5CD$ and $FG=2.25CD$, which of the following must be true?\n$AB=2.25EF$\n$FG=0.5AB$\n$\\frac{EF}{FG}=\\frac{AF}{FD}$","question_text_html":"<p><figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"356.889\" height=\"241.585\" viewBox=\"0 0 356.889 241.585\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A diagram of 2 lines and 4 line segments. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"bbe8e4d7-1e42-4547-9e03-1f6f4f13ea07\"><line x1=\"17.634\" y1=\"20.362\" x2=\"355.944\" y2=\"20.362\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><line x1=\"17.634\" y1=\"179.122\" x2=\"355.944\" y2=\"179.122\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><line x1=\"52.663\" y1=\"178.724\" x2=\"117.243\" y2=\"20.86\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><line x1=\"85.674\" y1=\"99.742\" x2=\"246.324\" y2=\"99.742\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><polyline points=\"312.864 20.86 182.134 178.722 117.243 20.86\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polyline><path d=\"M120.089,8.2V8.149q0-.009-.03-.039a.151.151,0,0,0-.077-.038c-.033-.007-.077-.013-.136-.02s-.135-.012-.232-.019l-.349-.019c-.136-.007-.3-.01-.484-.01h-.65q-.406,0-1.8.1a3.575,3.575,0,0,0-.524.775q-.465.776-.91,1.686a3.734,3.734,0,0,0-.446,1.2.438.438,0,0,0,.271.368,1.571,1.571,0,0,0,.5.194,2.09,2.09,0,0,0,.3.038c.026,0,.038.039.038.117a.905.905,0,0,1-.1.407q-1.8-.1-1.841-.1-.369,0-.649.019l-.611.039-.639.039a.219.219,0,0,1-.039-.155q0-.369.135-.369a2.15,2.15,0,0,0,.592-.116,1.158