55,4.552,4.552,0,0,1,1.095-3.218A3.586,3.586,0,0,1,307.82,228.735Zm-.195.718a1.707,1.707,0,0,0-1.541.862,2.919,2.919,0,0,0-.532,1.424c0,.091.038.136.116.136h3.78c.064,0,.1-.064.1-.194a2.717,2.717,0,0,0-.523-1.424A1.6,1.6,0,0,0,307.625,229.453Z\"></path><path d=\"M313.081,237.117a1.1,1.1,0,0,1-.339-.8,1.041,1.041,0,0,1,.339-.785,1.134,1.134,0,0,1,.805-.32,1.094,1.094,0,0,1,1.1,1.1,1.13,1.13,0,0,1-.321.8,1.036,1.036,0,0,1-.784.34A1.1,1.1,0,0,1,313.081,237.117Z\"></path></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 2 lines and 4 line segments\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>The 2 lines are labeled script l and j.<br><ul><li>Point upper A and point upper B are on line script l.</li><li>Point upper C and point upper D are on line j.</li></ul></li><li>Line segments upper A upper C, upper A upper D, and upper B upper D are drawn between line script l and line j.<br><ul><li>Point upper E is on line segment upper A upper C.</li><li>Point upper G is on line segment upper B upper D.</li></ul></li><li>Line segment upper E upper G is drawn from line segment upper A upper C to line segment upper B upper D.<br><ul><li>Line segment upper E upper G and line segment upper A upper D intersect at point upper F.</li></ul></li><li>The following 4 triangles are formed by the intersection of the 2 lines and 4 line segments:<br><ul><li>Triangle upper A upper C upper D</li><li>Triangle upper A upper E upper F</li><li>Triangle upper D upper B upper A</li><li>Triangle upper D upper F upper G</li></ul></li><li>3 angles are labeled as follows:<br><ul><li>The measure of angle upper A upper D upper C is x°.</li><li>The measure of angle upper A upper E upper F is x°.</li><li>The measure of 1 angle formed by the intersection of line script l and line segment upper A upper C and exterior to triangle upper A upper C upper D is x°.</li></ul></li><li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p><p></p><p>In the figure, $\\overline{EG}$ and $\\overline{AD}$ intersect at point $F$, and line $l$ is parallel to line $j$. If $EF=0.5CD$ and $FG=2.25CD$, which of the following must be true?</p><ol><li>$AB=2.25EF$</li><li>$FG=0.5AB$</li><li>$\\frac{EF}{FG}=\\frac{AF}{FD}$</li></ol>","choices":[{"label":"A","text":"I only"},{"label":"B","text":"II only"},{"label":"C","text":"I and II"},{"label":"D","text":"II and III"}],"correct_answer":"B","explanation":"Choice B is correct. In the figure, $\\overline{AE}$ intersects line $l$ and $\\overline{EG}$, and alternate interior angles are both marked $x^\\circ$. It follows that $\\overline{EG}$ is parallel to line $l$. It’s given that line $l$ is parallel to line $j$, so $\\overline{EG}$ is also parallel to line $j$. Thus, the following angles also have measure $x^\\circ$: $∠EFA$, $∠ACD$, $∠BAD$, and $∠GFD$. Triangles $AEF$ and $ACD$ each have two angles with measure $x^\\circ$, so triangles $AEF$ and $ACD$ are similar. It’s also given that $EF=0.5CD$, so $AF=0.5AD$. It follows that $AF=FD$. Triangles $DFG$ and $DAB$ each have one angle with measure $x^\\circ$ and share $∠FDG$, so triangles $DFG$ and $DAB$ are similar. Since $AF=FD$, it follows that $AD=2FD$, so $AB=2FG$. Substituting $2FG$ for $AB$ in statement I yields $2FG=2.25EF$. It's given that $FG=2.25CD$. Substituting $2.25CD$ for $FG$ and $0.5CD$ for $EF$ in the equation $2FG=2.25EF$ yields $2(2.25CD)=2.25(0.5CD)$, or $4.5CD=1.125CD$. Thus, statement I is not true. Since $AB=2FG$, it follows that $0.5AB=FG$, or $FG=0.5AB$. Therefore, statement II must be true. Substituting $0.5CD$ for $EF$, $2.25CD$ for $FG$, and $FD$ for $AF$ in statement III yields $\\frac{0.5CD}{2.25CD}=\\frac{FD}{FD}$, or $\\frac{2}{9}=1$. Thus, statement III is not true. Therefore, statement II only must be true.\nChoice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.\nChoice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.\nChoice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.","is_grid_in":false},{"source_id":"de9148c4","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"easy","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"A right triangle. Refer to long description.\nWhich equation shows the relationship between the side lengths of the triangle shown?","question_text_html":"<p><figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"250.0pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 250.0 210.0\" height=\"210.0pt\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A right triangle. Refer to long description.\"><g><g><defs></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 207.871875 L 248.4 207.871875 L 248.4 0 L 0 0 L 0 207.871875 z \" style=\"fill: none\"></path></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 7.2 198 L 241.2 198 L 241.2 7.2 L 7.2 7.2 L 7.2 198 z \" style=\"fill: none\"></path></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g transform=\"translate(222.48 102.6) scale(0.18 -0.18)\"><defs><path id=\"STIXGeneral-Regular-33\" d=\"M 390 3264 L 288 3290 Q 435 3770 748 4048 Q 1062 4326 1542 4326 Q 1990 4326 2265 4083 Q 2541 3840 2541 3450 Q 2541 2925 1946 2566 Q 2298 2413 2477 2227 Q 2758 1914 2758 1402 Q 2758 890 2464 506 Q 2246 211 1840 60 Q 1434 -90 979 -90 Q 262 -90 262 275 Q 262 378 339 442 Q 416 506 525 506 Q 685 506 915 339 Q 1197 141 1466 141 Q 1818 141 2058 425 Q 2298 710 2298 1120 Q 2298 1856 1632 2048 Q 1434 2112 979 2112 L 979 2202 Q 1338 2323 1517 2432 Q 2035 2726 2035 3290 Q 2035 3610 1852 3776 Q 1670 3942 1344 3942 Q 768 3942 390 3264 z \" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Regular-33\" transform=\"translate(0 0.40625)\"></use></g></g><g id=\"text_2\"><g transform=\"translate(115.2 182.736) scale(0.18 -0.18)\"><defs><path id=\"STIXGeneral-Regular-31\" d=\"M 2522 0 L 755 0 L 755 96 Q 1107 115 1235 227 Q 1363 339 1363 608 L 1363 3482 Q 1363 3795 1171 37