819,82.251,224.509,82.264,225.3,82.264Z\" fill=\"#231f20\"></path><path d=\"M134.869,188.157a15.8,15.8,0,0,1,4.128.872q-.35,2.211-.388,2.4-.057.291-.465.291a.3.3,0,0,1-.213-.059c0-.193-.007-.368-.019-.522a2.655,2.655,0,0,0-.195-.679,2.034,2.034,0,0,0-.474-.736,2.659,2.659,0,0,0-.94-.524,4.5,4.5,0,0,0-1.531-.232,4.844,4.844,0,0,0-3.721,2.132,7.651,7.651,0,0,0-1.724,4.96,4.679,4.679,0,0,0,1.007,3.082,3.486,3.486,0,0,0,2.849,1.221,4.477,4.477,0,0,0,2.442-.639,3.537,3.537,0,0,0,.842-.7,6.062,6.062,0,0,0,.524-.658,1.235,1.235,0,0,1,.184-.252c.039,0,.117.068.233.2s.168.23.155.282q-.873,1.666-.97,1.763a3.059,3.059,0,0,1-1.51.581,12.159,12.159,0,0,1-2.462.252,4.636,4.636,0,0,1-3.682-1.579,5.467,5.467,0,0,1-1.376-3.712,6.9,6.9,0,0,1,.571-2.654,9.647,9.647,0,0,1,1.522-2.51,7.611,7.611,0,0,1,2.335-1.86A6.1,6.1,0,0,1,134.869,188.157Z\" fill=\"#231f20\"></path></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for triangle upper A upper B upper C and triangle upper B upper D upper E\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Triangle upper A upper B upper C is labeled as follows:<br><ul><li>Angle upper A upper B upper C is a right angle.</li><li>The length of side upper A upper B is r.</li></ul></li><li>Triangle upper B upper D upper E is labeled as follows:<br><ul><li>Angle upper B upper D upper E is a right angle.</li><li>The length of side upper D upper E is s.</li></ul></li><li>The 2 triangles partially overlap:<br><ul><li>Side upper A upper C of triangle upper A upper B upper C intersects side upper B upper E of triangle upper B upper D upper E.</li><li>Vertex upper C of triangle upper A upper B upper C lies on side upper B upper D of triangle upper B upper D upper E.</li></ul></li><li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p><p></p><p>In the figure shown, $△ABC$ is congruent to $△BDE$. If $r=54$ and $s=26$, what is the length of $CD$?</p>","choices":[{"label":"A","text":"$26$"},{"label":"B","text":"$27$"},{"label":"C","text":"$28$"},{"label":"D","text":"$54$"}],"correct_answer":"C","explanation":"Choice C is correct. It’s given that $△ABC$ is congruent to $△BDE$. Corresponding sides of congruent triangles are equal in length. It’s given that $r$, which represents the length of $\\overline{AB}$, is equal to $54$ and $s$, which represents the length of $\\overline{DE}$, is equal to $26$. Since $\\overline{AB}$ and $\\overline{DE}$ aren’t equal in length, it follows that $\\overline{AB}$ corresponds to $\\overline{BD}$ and $\\overline{BC}$ corresponds to $\\overline{DE}$. Therefore, the length of $\\overline{BD}$ is $54$ and the length of $\\overline{BC}$ is $26$. The points $B$, $C$, and $D$ lie on a straight line, so the length of $\\overline{BD}$ can be expressed as the sum of the lengths of $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{CD}$. This relationship can be written as $BD=BC+CD$. Substituting $54$ for $BD$ and $26$ for $BC$ in this equation yields $54=26+CD$. Subtracting $26$ from both sides of this equation yields $CD=28$. Therefore, the length of $\\overline{CD}$ is $28$.\nChoice A is incorrect. This is the length of $\\overline{BC}$, not $\\overline{CD}$.\nChoice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.\nChoice D is incorrect. This is the length of $\\overline{BD}$, not $\\overline{CD}$.","is_grid_in":false},{"source_id":"4757123b","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Area and volume","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"Trapezoid A and trapezoid B are similar. The length of each side of trapezoid A is $41$ times the length of the corresponding side of trapezoid B. The area of trapezoid A is how many times as large as the area of trapezoid B?","question_text_html":null,"choices":[],"correct_answer":"1681","explanation":"The correct answer is $1,681$. It’s given that trapezoid A and trapezoid B are similar. When two trapezoids are similar, the scale factor between their corresponding side lengths is $k$, and the scale factor between their areas is $k^2$. It’s given that the length of each side of trapezoid A is $41$ times the length of the corresponding side of trapezoid B, so the scale factor between their corresponding side lengths is $41$. It follows that the scale factor between the areas is $41^2$, or $1,681$. Therefore, the area of trapezoid A is $1,681$ times as large as the area of trapezoid B.","is_grid_in":true},{"source_id":"ffc39dc5","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"medium","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"Quadrilateral upper C upper D upper E upper F. Refer to long description.\nIn the figure shown, $CD=EF$ and $FC=DE$. If $x=65$ and $y=30$, what is the measure of $∠CDE$?","question_text_html":"<p><figure><svg id=\"uuid-a21e70b7-4fe2-422a-b825-aa42d121ba90\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"247.442\" height=\"253.856\" viewBox=\"0 0 247.442 253.856\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Quadrilateral upper C upper D upper E upper F. Refer to long description.\"><polygon points=\"184.94 190.29 31.982 190.29 62.667 18.3 215.626 18.3 184.94 190.29\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><line x1=\"62.577\" y1=\"18.172\" x2=\"185.031\" y2=\"190.418\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><path d=\"m55.714.116c1.679,0,2.952.465,3.817,1.396s1.299,2.1,1.299,3.508c0,.659-.097,1.344-.291,2.054s-.5,1.415-.92,2.112-.92,1.324-1.502,1.88-1.298,1.005-2.151,1.347c-.853.343-1.777.514-2.771.514-.232,0-.691-.016-1.376-.048-.685-.032-1.247-.048-1.686-.048l-2.151.097c-.013-.013-.019-.064-.019-.155,0-.246.032-.369.097-.369.142,0,.381-.051.717-.155.335-.104.529-.213.581-.33.181-.375.349-.975.504-1.802l1.396-7.209c.167-.917.239-1.518.213-1.802-.013-.103-.162-.207-.445-.31-.285-.103-.498-.155-.64-.155-.026,0-.039-.026-.039-.078,0-.207.045-.355.136-.446.594.026,1.286.039,2.074.039.452,0,1.034-.006,1.