3-.322.698-.115.225-.24.46-.375.704-.135.246-.292.523-.472.833l-2.955,5.085c-.1.18-.172.338-.217.473-.045.135-.068.258-.068.367,0,.19.07.328.21.413s.35.127.63.127h.345l-.12.63H0Zm3.51-3.585v-.75h4.889v.75H3.51Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><path d=\"m123.181,264.798l.12-.63h.194c.22,0,.428-.022.623-.067.194-.045.364-.14.51-.285.145-.145.252-.362.322-.652l1.575-7.425c.02-.061.035-.135.045-.226.01-.09.015-.154.015-.194,0-.26-.1-.425-.3-.495s-.46-.105-.78-.105h-.194l.135-.63h7.56l-.479,2.625h-.78c.01-.109.02-.228.03-.353.01-.125.02-.237.029-.337.011-.101.016-.16.016-.181,0-.29-.083-.529-.248-.72-.165-.189-.457-.285-.877-.285h-2.46l-.93,4.335h3.614l-.149.735h-3.615l-.675,3.18c-.01.07-.021.138-.03.203-.01.064-.015.122-.015.172,0,.311.103.505.308.585.204.08.447.12.728.12h.494l-.119.63h-4.665Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><path d=\"m249.549,264.948c-.87,0-1.612-.157-2.228-.473-.614-.315-1.087-.772-1.417-1.372-.33-.601-.495-1.325-.495-2.176,0-.89.145-1.752.435-2.587s.708-1.583,1.253-2.243c.545-.659,1.197-1.185,1.957-1.574.761-.391,1.606-.585,2.536-.585.889,0,1.574.152,2.055.457.48.306.721.708.721,1.208,0,.359-.137.645-.406.854s-.625.315-1.064.315c0-.21-.018-.433-.053-.668-.035-.234-.105-.457-.209-.667-.105-.21-.256-.38-.451-.511-.195-.13-.457-.194-.787-.194-.551,0-1.053.133-1.508.397s-.86.62-1.215,1.064c-.355.445-.652.948-.893,1.508-.24.561-.423,1.138-.548,1.732s-.188,1.173-.188,1.732c0,.59.1,1.095.3,1.515.2.421.498.74.893.961.396.22.888.329,1.479.329.709,0,1.287-.142,1.732-.427s.793-.598,1.043-.938c.059.04.107.104.143.194.033.091.051.19.051.301,0,.26-.107.534-.322.824s-.553.533-1.012.728c-.461.195-1.061.293-1.801.293Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><polygon points=\"127.92 17.698 14.038 248.35 241.803 248.35 127.92 17.698\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\"></polygon><line x1=\"127.92\" y1=\"18.35\" x2=\"127.92\" y2=\"248.35\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line><line x1=\"56.92\" y1=\"161.35\" x2=\"198.92\" y2=\"161.35\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line><line x1=\"14.038\" y1=\"248.658\" x2=\"127.92\" y2=\"161.35\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for triangle upper A upper B upper C\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Line segment upper D upper E is drawn from side upper A upper B to side upper B upper C.</li><li>Line segment upper B upper F is drawn from point upper B to side upper A upper C.</li><li>Line segment upper D upper E and line segment upper B upper F intersect at point upper O.</li><li>Line segment upper A upper O is drawn from point upper A to point upper O.</li><li>The measure of angle upper O upper A upper C is 30°.</li><li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p><p></p><p>In triangle $ABC$, $AB=BC$. Points $D$ and $E$ lie on line segments $AB$ and $BC$, respectively, such that line segments $DE$ and $AC$ are parallel. Point $O$ is the midpoint of line segment $DE$, and the measure of $∠OAC$ is $30^\\circ$. Point $F$ lies on line segment $AC$, and line segment $BF$ passes through point $O$. If $AB=81$ and $AO=BO$, what is the length of line segment $BE$?</p>","choices":[],"correct_answer":"54","explanation":"The correct answer is $54$. It's given that $AB=BC$, so triangle $ABC$ is isosceles. It's also given that line segments $DE$ and $AC$ are parallel. Since line segments $DE$ and $AC$ are parallel, triangle $BDE$ is similar to triangle $BAC$, which means triangle $BDE$ is also isosceles. It’s given that point $O$ is the midpoint of line segment $DE$. Since triangle $BDE$ is isosceles, line segment $BO$ splits triangle $BDE$ into two congruent triangles, where $∠BOD$ is a right angle. Therefore, $∠BFA$ is also a right angle. The figure shows that the measure of $∠OAF$ is $30^\\circ$. It follows that triangle $AOF$ is a 30-60-90 triangle, where the measure of $∠AOF$ is $60^\\circ$. In a 30-60-90 triangle, the side opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle is half the length of the side opposite the $90^\\circ$ angle. Let $x$ represent the length of line segment $OF$ and let $2x$ represent the length of line segment $AO$. It's given that $AO=BO$. Since $AO=BO$, the length of line segment $BO$ is also $2x$. It follows that the length of line segment $BF$ is $BO+OF$, which is $2x+x$, or $3x$. Since triangle $BDE$ is similar to triangle $BAC$, the ratio of corresponding side lengths is equal to the ratio of the heights of the triangles. This means that $\\frac{BE}{BC}=\\frac{BO}{BF}$. Substituting $2x$ for $BO$ and $3x$ for $BF$ in this equation yields $\\frac{BE}{BC}=\\frac{2x}{3x}$, or $\\frac{BE}{BC}=\\frac{2}{3}$. It’s given that $AB=81$ and $AB=BC$, so $BC=81$. Substituting $81$ for $BC$ in the equation $\\frac{BE}{BC}=\\frac{2}{3}$ yields $\\frac{BE}{81}=\\frac{2}{3}$. Multiplying both sides of this equation by $81$ yields $BE=\\frac{2}{3}(81)$, or $BE=54$.","is_grid_in":true},{"source_id":"10e059a6","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Circles","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"The measure of angle $A$ is $\\frac{π}{216}$ radians. The measure of angle $B$ is $36$ times the measure of angle $A$. What is the value of $\\cosB$?","question_text_html":null,"choices":[{"label":"A","text":"$0$"},{"label":"B","text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$"},{"label":"C","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$"},{"label":"D","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$"}],"correct_answer":"D","explanation":"Choice D is correct. It’s given that the measure of angle $A$ is $\\frac{π}{216}$ radians and the measure of angle $B$ is $36$ times the measure of angle $A$. Therefore, the measure of angle $B$ is $36(\\frac{π}{216})$ radians, or $\\frac{π}{6}$ radians. A trigonometric ratio can be found using the unit circle, or a circle with radius $1$ unit. For a unit circle centered at the origin in the xy-plane, the cosine of $\\frac{π}{6}$ radians is the x-coordinate of the point resulting from traveling a distance of $\\frac{π}{6}$ counterclockwise from the point $(1,0)$. This results in the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$. Therefore, the value of $\\cosB$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nChoice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.\nChoice B is incorrect. This is the value of $\\sinB$, not $\\cosB$.\nChoice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.","is_grid_in":false},{"source_id":"9f9112ab","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Circles","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"The measure of angle $L$ is $60$ degrees. If the measure of angle $L$ is $\\frac{π}{n}$ radians, where $n$ is a constant, what is the value of $n$?","question_text_html":null,"choices":[],"correct_answer":"3","explanation":"The correct answer is $3$. The measure of an angle in radians is equal to the measure of the angle in degrees multiplied by $\\frac{π}{180}$. It’s given that the measure of angle $L$ is $60$ degrees. Multiplying $60$ by $\\frac{π}{180}$ yields $\\frac{60π}{180}$, or $\\frac{π}{3}$. It’s also given that the measure of angle $L$ is $\\frac{π}{n}$ radians, so $\\frac{π}{n}=\\frac{π}{3}$. Dividing both sides of this equation by $π$ yields $\\frac{1}{n}=\\frac{1}{3}$. Taking the reciprocal of both sides of this equation yields $\\frac{n}{1}=\\frac{3}{1}$, or $n=3$. Therefore, the value of $n$ is $3$.","is_grid_in":true},{"source_id":"6c67dd47","section":"math","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"hard","passage":null,"passage_html":null,"question_text":"Triangle upper X upper Y upper Z. Refer to long description.\nIn the figure shown, the measure of angle $X$ is $54^\\circ$. The length of $XY$ is $26$ units and the length of $XZ$ is $19$ units. What is the area, in square units, of triangle $XYZ$?","question_text_htm